WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.750
- I'm here with Jessica St. Clair,

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.069
June Diane Raphael,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.129
Sasheer Zamata, Nicole Byer,

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:06.789
my friend Sheea Shafer,

00:00:06.789 --> 00:00:09.670
and our whole audience full of besties.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.500
In fact, our next incredible story

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.810
comes from a pair of women
in our audience right now.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.460
Their friendship was purely built

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.780
on the power of handwritten letters.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.820
It's exactly the kind of
story our friends at Pilot,

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.920
makers of the G2 Gelling Pen,

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.570
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.900
love to help us celebrate.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.780
47 years ago, they were in fifth grade,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.420
one living in Idaho,
the other in Louisiana,

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.390
and they became pen pals.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.370
What started as a school project

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.950
turned into hundreds of letters

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.190
that went from grade
school through college,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.890
marriages and kids.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.620
And what's really crazy is,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.890
although they'll always
be the best of friends,

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.850
they've actually only met
in person three times.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.260
Well, four, if you count today.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.049
Let's say hi to Kathy
and London, everybody!

00:00:52.049 --> 00:00:54.548
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:54.548 --> 00:00:55.381
Hello!

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.587
So meet everybody, first of all

00:00:58.587 --> 00:00:59.420
- Hey!

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.253
- [Nicole] Hey!

00:01:00.253 --> 00:01:01.270
- So how did this-

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.103
So it began-

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:03.410
I had a pen pal, actually, in school

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.450
and it was like the coolest thing ever

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:05.770
and that's how this started, right?

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.410
- So, so our start,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.960
mine started with a teacher assignment

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.790
and we had to pick a state.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:12.660
And I guess

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.600
I picked Idaho

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.580
because it was a boot

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.960
and Louisiana was a boot as well.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.590
And we had to do research on it

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.580
and then kind of the crowning point of it

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.451
was we wrote a letter to a student

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.550
and all the letters were collected,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.250
they went to a school district in Idaho

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.470
and then I waited to see
if I would get a letter

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.640
and it ended up with Kathy
and she wrote back to me.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.473
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:01:36.473 --> 00:01:38.102
So how did it come across to you, Kathy?

00:01:38.102 --> 00:01:40.010
Did you wanna do this or your teacher,

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:40.843
it was the same kind of assignment?

00:01:40.843 --> 00:01:42.840
- Well, it was very casual handoff

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.510
that actually came from a friend

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.200
who apparently had been handed the letter

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.150
and didn't want it.

00:01:48.465 --> 00:01:49.925
So, you know, handed it to me

00:01:49.925 --> 00:01:52.970
and I reached out, wrote
a letter right away

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.740
and it's always a good sign

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.490
when the person you're
writing writes back.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.070
And so that really kind of started us off

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.590
and we traded letters back
and forth really regularly.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.610
You know, there's just
nothing quite as thrilling

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.550
as getting a letter in the mail

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.410
that someone has handwritten,
so it was awesome.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.440
- [Kelly] Yeah, I mean
and it must have been

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.910
pretty powerful letters

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.640
because y'all have only
hung out a few times.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.210
So like, I mean over the years, like,

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:18.710
do you really, is it,
do you find it easier?

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.170
It's almost like easier
to like write it out

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.003
and have that-

00:02:22.003 --> 00:02:24.320
It's a different kind of
connection, I feel like.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.030
- It's really like having a conversation

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:29.007
but a really slow, patient conversation

00:02:29.007 --> 00:02:30.520
that we've had over the years

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.510
that we've gotten to know each other.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.240
And it is very powerful.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.803
We have found that we
have a lot in common.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.840
We both grew up in small towns

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.290
and we kind of went through
high school together,

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.120
you know writing about dating and clubs

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.640
and school and studying,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.800
and then college and what
was the future for us,

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.270
and then our spouses and children,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.100
now grandchildren, so.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:56.933
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:02:56.933 --> 00:02:57.796
That's so cool.

00:02:57.796 --> 00:03:00.310
(audience applauding)

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.248
Have y'all, did you ever
have pen pals growing up?

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.570
- I never had a pen pal.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.600
I mean, I love the idea of it,

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.790
I think it's so beautiful,

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.740
but I struggle with,

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.550
as Jessica knows, I
struggle with communication

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.550
and responding to texts.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.130
- I write back to every
single fan we have on DM

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.107
and they'll send me things
for June and I'm like,

00:03:16.107 --> 00:03:17.760
"I'll get it to her right away."

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.110
Like, I'm her social secretary!

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.990
- Well, but the two of us really resent

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.708
other friends we have
who leave us voicemails.

00:03:24.708 --> 00:03:25.541
- Ugh.

00:03:25.541 --> 00:03:26.374
- That, to me is-

00:03:26.374 --> 00:03:27.207
- We hate voicemails!

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:28.290
- In this day and age, unacceptable.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.280
I'd rather a letter!

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.252
- I'd rather you fax me!
- Yeah!

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:33.214
- I don't wanna check it!

00:03:33.214 --> 00:03:34.563
- [Sasheer] Wait, why
do yo hate voicemails?

00:03:34.563 --> 00:03:36.147
- How dare you send me a voicemail!

00:03:36.147 --> 00:03:37.863
- Oh, I'm so angry right now.

00:03:38.948 --> 00:03:39.781
So angry.

00:03:39.781 --> 00:03:42.033
- The effort it takes me to dial into that

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.310
- And, the fear.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.151
- And the fear!

00:03:44.151 --> 00:03:44.984
- [Kelly] No, wait, now you do-

00:03:44.984 --> 00:03:46.332
- You don't have to dial
into the voicemail anymore.

00:03:46.332 --> 00:03:48.072
- No, you can just press the button.

00:03:48.072 --> 00:03:50.481
- And they transcribe
it for you like a text.

00:03:50.481 --> 00:03:52.310
- Or, or they have the
thing where you text,

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.143
and you just hold down the thing

00:03:53.143 --> 00:03:53.976
and you say it and then
it sends the voice.

00:03:53.976 --> 00:03:55.530
- I like a voice memo!
- [Sasheer] Yeah.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.580
- I hate a voicemail.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.107
- [Shasheer] Oh wow.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:58.107 --> 00:03:58.940
- Important distinction!

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.403
- Important!

00:04:00.403 --> 00:04:01.610
- Nicole leaves me...
[Nicole Chuckling]

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.710
My whole inbox is just Nicole

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.060
leaving me crazy voice memos.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.108
But I love it
(audience clapping)

00:04:06.108 --> 00:04:08.452
because she's just like,
"hi, wada dada dada,"

00:04:08.452 --> 00:04:10.353
like, make voices,
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:10.353 --> 00:04:13.561
and like, alright, I'll just
listen to this for two minutes.

00:04:13.561 --> 00:04:15.100
- And then whenever her
voicemail box is full,

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.400
I then leave, like, an audio message,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.432
like via text, and be like,

00:04:18.432 --> 00:04:19.681
"it's full! Why?!"
- [Kelly] Why is it full?!

00:04:19.681 --> 00:04:21.114
- Yeah.

00:04:21.114 --> 00:04:22.003
- It's full of you!

00:04:22.003 --> 00:04:24.000
- Nicole, don't ever leave me a voicemail.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.573
- [Nicole] I really want to now!

00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:26.406
- Please, don't!

00:04:26.406 --> 00:04:27.239
- We'll never hear it!
- They're fun!

00:04:27.239 --> 00:04:29.210
- I've had the United States government

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.174
leaving me voicemails

00:04:30.174 --> 00:04:31.470
and you know what?
- [Nicole] What did you do?!

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.670
- Who knows!

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:33.503
There has to be...

00:04:33.503 --> 00:04:35.060
If it's important enough,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.993
they will find other avenues.
- [Shaheer] Other ways.

00:04:36.993 --> 00:04:38.713
(everyone laughing)
(audience clapping)

00:04:38.713 --> 00:04:40.170
- Alright.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.540
- Well, like I said earlier,

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.310
our season long partner, Pilot G2,

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.630
the go-to pen of The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.580
loves to celebrate long
lasting friendships

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.320
built on the power of writing.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.560
So to honor your incredible friendship,

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.110
they're gonna give you $5,000

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.648
to help plan your ultimate girls getaway.

00:04:53.648 --> 00:04:54.481
(audience clapping)

00:04:54.481 --> 00:04:55.632
- Oh!
- Oh my God!

00:04:55.632 --> 00:04:56.672
- [Kelly] Exactly!

00:04:56.672 --> 00:04:58.422
- That's incredible!

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.900
- [Kelly] They're also gonna give you

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.950
a basket of Pilot pens because

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.412
I'm assuming you like writing
letters, so they're like...

00:05:08.412 --> 00:05:09.245
- [London] Thank you.

00:05:09.245 --> 00:05:10.745
Thank you, Kelly!

